---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="What is Krillion? The Viral Reverse-Trivia Deep Sea Game Explained - Krillion.si"
  description="What is Krillion? Learn how the viral ocean trench trivia game works, why common answers drown at the surface, how the 7,000m scoring system works, and how to play online."
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 prose prose-invert prose-cyan">
    <!-- Breadcrumb & Header -->
    <div class="mb-8">
      <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-abyss-cyan mb-2">Explainer & FAQ</div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black text-white leading-tight">
        What is Krillion? The Reverse-Trivia Trench Diver Explained
      </h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm mt-3">
        By Krillion Explainer Desk • Updated October 2026 • 5 min read
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Quick Definition Box (Optimized for Google Featured Snippet) -->
    <div class="bg-abyss-card border border-cyan-500/30 rounded-2xl p-6 my-8 not-prose space-y-3 shadow-lg shadow-cyan-950/20">
      <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-abyss-cyan flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <span>📖</span> Quick Definition
      </div>
      <p class="text-base text-slate-200 leading-relaxed font-medium">
        <strong>Krillion</strong> is a daily online reverse-trivia game where players dive into a simulated deep-sea ocean trench by answering factual prompts. Unlike standard trivia games that reward speed and popular facts, Krillion awards <strong>depth</strong> based on <em>rarity</em>: the more common your answer is among other players, the shallower you remain (0m–1,500m). Valid but obscure answers plunge you down to the <strong>7,000-meter Hadal Abyss</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>How Does the Krillion Game Work?</h2>
    <p>
      In a standard daily round of Krillion, players are presented with a series of <strong>7 category prompts</strong> spanning World History, Global Geography, Literature, Science, and Cinema.
    </p>
    <p>
      For each prompt, you have 60 seconds to submit a single valid answer. The game's engine tests your answer across four distinct depth tiers:
    </p>

    <!-- Visual Tier Comparison Table -->
    <div class="not-prose my-8 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-xs text-left bg-abyss-card rounded-2xl border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
        <thead class="bg-white/5 uppercase text-slate-400">
          <tr>
            <th class="p-3.5">Zone & Depth</th>
            <th class="p-3.5">Answer Type</th>
            <th class="p-3.5">Example (Prompt: Roman Emperor)</th>
            <th class="p-3.5">Why It Scores This Way</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/5">
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-blue-400">0m - 1,500m<br /><span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 font-normal">Sunlight Surface Floater</span></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-300">Pop-culture consensus</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-medium text-white"><em>Augustus, Julius Caesar, Nero</em></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-400">Chosen by 60%+ of participants; excessive crowd consensus prevents diving.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-amber-400">2,500m - 4,500m<br /><span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 font-normal">Too-Clever Crowd Trap</span></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-300">Textbook "smart" answer</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-medium text-white"><em>Caligula, Marcus Aurelius, Hadrian</em></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-400">Intelligent players think nobody else will choose it, causing a mid-depth cluster.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-cyan-300">5,000m - 6,500m<br /><span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 font-normal">Bathyal Trench Sinker</span></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-300">Secondary historical fact</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-medium text-white"><em>Diocletian, Probus, Majorian</em></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-400">Genuine rarity with very few daily participants guessing it.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-abyss-cyan">7,000m (Max Depth)<br /><span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 font-normal">Hadal Abyss Crown 👑</span></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-300">Ultra-niche valid archival footnote</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-medium text-white"><em>Didius Julianus, Pertinax, Gordian I</em></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-400">Under 0.05% selection rate. Unlocks maximum depth and viral bragging rights.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Why is Krillion So Addictive?</h2>
    <p>
      Krillion turns traditional trivia on its head by introducing <strong>psychological game theory</strong>:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cognitive Second-Guessing:</strong> You can't just know a fact; you must anticipate what <em>other players know</em> and actively veer away from consensus.</li>
      <li><strong>The "Too-Clever" Agony:</strong> Getting trapped at 3,200m with an answer you thought was a genius secret creates immense drive to replay and refine your strategy.</li>
      <li><strong>Viral Daily Share Grids:</strong> Like Wordle, players share an emoji depth grid (e.g. <code>👑👑⚠️🌊👑</code>) across social platforms to compare their total depth out of 49,000 meters.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where Can You Play Krillion?</h2>
    <p>
      You can play instantly right here on <strong>Krillion.si</strong>:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong><a href="/daily" class="text-abyss-cyan font-semibold">Daily Dive</a>:</strong> 7 official prompts updated each calendar day.</li>
      <li><strong><a href="/endless" class="text-abyss-cyan font-semibold">Endless Mode</a>:</strong> Unlimited practice rounds with zero waiting periods, perfect for training your 7,000m instinct.</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- Bottom CTA Bar -->
    <div class="mt-12 p-8 rounded-3xl bg-abyss-card border border-cyan-500/30 text-center not-prose space-y-4">
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-white">Ready to Plunge Into the Abyss?</h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 max-w-md mx-auto">
        Test your obscurity instincts now in our browser arena. No sign-up or download required.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4 pt-2">
        <a href="/daily" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-abyss-cyan to-blue-600 text-abyss-dark font-extrabold text-sm hover:scale-105 active:scale-95 transition-all shadow-lg shadow-abyss-cyan/20">
          Play Today's Daily Dive ⚓
        </a>
        <a href="/endless" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-2xl bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold text-sm transition-all border border-white/10">
          Try Endless Practice ♾️
        </a>
        <a href="https://krillionhints.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-2xl bg-amber-500/20 hover:bg-amber-500/30 text-amber-300 font-bold text-sm transition-all border border-amber-500/30">
          Daily Solver on KrillionHints.com ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
